What is claimed is: 

         1 . A device for amplifying radio frequency (RF) signals, the device comprising:
 a planar dielectric substrate comprising:
 a metallized top side; 
 a metallized bottom side; 
 a first hollow conductive slot forming an input substrate waveguide between the metallized top side and the metallized bottom side; 
 a first substrate-integrated waveguide (SIW) forming an N-way splitter located after the first conductive slot; 
 N power amplifiers located after the splitter; 
 a second SIW located after the N power amplifiers and forming an N-way combiner; and 
 a second hollow conductive slot located after the N-way combiner and forming an output substrate waveguide between the metallized top side and the metallized bottom side; 
   a heat sink comprising:
 an input socket; 
 a heat sink input waveguide aligned with the input socket and the input substrate waveguide; 
 an output socket; and 
 a heat sink output waveguide aligned with the output socket and the output substrate waveguide. 



         2 . The device of  claim 1 , further comprising:
 an input external waveguide affixed to the input socket and aligned with the heat sink input waveguide; and   an output external waveguide affixed to the output socket and aligned with the heat sink output waveguide.   


         3 . The device of  claim 2 , wherein the input socket or the output socket is located on a bottom face of the heat sink, such that the input external waveguide or the output external waveguide extends in a direction perpendicular to the planar dielectric substrate. 


         4 . The device of  claim 2 , wherein the input socket or the output socket is located on a side face of the heat sink, such that the input external waveguide or the output external waveguide extends in a direction parallel to the planar dielectric substrate. 


         5 . The device of  claim 1 , wherein the planar dielectric substrate comprises glass. 


         6 . The device of  claim 1 , wherein at least one of the heat sink input waveguide, the input substrate waveguide, the first SIW, the second SIW, the output substrate waveguide, or the heat sink output waveguide comprises air. 


         7 . The device of  claim 1 , wherein the N power amplifiers comprise N microwave monolithic integrated circuits (MMICs), and wherein the planar dielectric substrate includes cavities such that the MMICs are in direct contact with the heat sink. 


         8 . A method for amplifying a radio frequency (RF) signal, the method comprising:
 providing a planar dielectric substrate comprising a metallized top side and a metallized bottom side;   with a first hollow conductive slot, forming an input substrate waveguide between the metallized top side and the metallized bottom side;   with a first substrate-integrated waveguide (SIW), forming an N-way splitter located after the first conductive slot;   providing N power amplifiers located after the splitter;   with a second SIW located after the N power amplifiers, forming an N-way combiner;   with a second hollow conductive slot located after the N-way combiner, forming an output substrate waveguide between the metallized top side and the metallized bottom side;   providing a heat sink comprising:
 an input socket; 
 a heat sink input waveguide aligned with the input socket and the input substrate waveguide; 
 an output socket; 
 a heat sink output waveguide aligned with the output socket and the output substrate waveguide; 
 receiving the RF signal via the input socket, heat sink input waveguide, and the input substrate waveguide; 
 amplifying the RF signal using the N-way splitter, the N power amplifiers, and the N-way combiner to generate an amplified RF signal; and 
 transmitting the amplified RF signal through the output substrate waveguide, heat sink output waveguide, and output socket. 



         9 . The method of  claim 8 , further comprising:
 affixing an input external waveguide affixed to the input socket such that the input external waveguide is aligned with the heat sink input waveguide; and   affixing an output external waveguide affixed to the output socket such that the output external waveguide is aligned with the heat sink output waveguide.   


         10 . The method of  claim 9 , wherein the input socket or the output socket is located on a bottom face of the heat sink, such that the input external waveguide or the output external waveguide extends in a direction perpendicular to the planar dielectric substrate. 


         11 . The method of  claim 9 , wherein the input socket or the output socket is located on a side face of the heat sink, such that the input external waveguide or the output external waveguide extends in a direction parallel to the planar dielectric substrate. 


         12 . The method of  claim 8 , wherein the planar dielectric substrate comprises glass. 


         13 . The method of  claim 8 , wherein at least one of the heat sink input waveguide, the input substrate waveguide, the first SIW, the second SIW, the output substrate waveguide, or the heat sink output waveguide comprises air. 


         14 . The method of  claim 9 , wherein the N power amplifiers comprise N microwave monolithic integrated circuits (MMICs) , and wherein the planar dielectric substrate includes cavities such that the MMICs are in direct contact with the heat sink. 


         15 . A wireless device comprising:
 an amplification device comprising:
 a planar dielectric substrate comprising:
 a metallized top side; 
 a metallized bottom side; 
 a first hollow conductive slot forming an input substrate waveguide between the metallized top side and the metallized bottom side; 
 a first substrate-integrated waveguide (SIW) forming an N-way splitter located after the first conductive slot; 
 N power amplifiers located after the splitter; 
 a second SIW located after the N power amplifiers and forming an N-way combiner; and 
 a second hollow conductive slot located after the N-way combiner and forming an output substrate waveguide between the metallized top side and the metallized bottom side; 

 a heat sink comprising:
 an input socket; 
 a heat sink input waveguide aligned with the input socket and the input substrate waveguide; 
 an output socket; and 
 a heat sink output waveguide aligned with the output socket and the output substrate waveguide. 




         16 . The wireless device of  claim 15 , further comprising:
 an input external waveguide affixed to the input socket and aligned with the heat sink input waveguide; and   an output external waveguide affixed to the output socket and aligned with the heat sink output waveguide.   


         17 . The wireless device of  claim 16 , wherein the input socket or the output socket is located on a bottom face of the heat sink, such that the input external waveguide or the output external waveguide extends in a direction perpendicular to the planar dielectric substrate. 


         18 . The wireless device of  claim 16 , wherein the input socket or the output socket is located on a side face of the heat sink, such that the input external waveguide or the output external waveguide extends in a direction parallel to the planar dielectric substrate. 


         19 . The wireless device of  claim 15 , wherein the planar dielectric substrate comprises glass. 


         20 . The wireless device of  claim 15 , wherein at least one of the heat sink input waveguide, the input substrate waveguide, the first SIW, the second SIW, the output substrate waveguide, or the heat sink output waveguide comprises air.

