1 . A power transmission apparatus comprising:
 a plurality of coils, wherein two or more coils among the plurality of coils are arranged along a first direction, and two or more coils among the plurality of coils are arranged along a second direction different from the first direction; and   a unit configured to:
 execute a process of a Ping; 
 obtain, from a first power receiving apparatus, a first signal strength packet including a value related to a received power after the process of the Ping is executed for the first power receiving apparatus; 
 obtain, from the first power receiving apparatus, first identification information of the first power receiving apparatus after the first signal strength packet is obtained; 
 obtain, from a second power receiving apparatus, a second signal strength packet including a value related to a received power after the process of the Ping is executed for the second power receiving apparatus; 
 obtain, from the second power receiving apparatus, second identification information of the second power receiving apparatus after the second signal strength packet is obtained; 
 wirelessly perform power transfer to the first power receiving apparatus via a first coil which is included in the plurality of coils and which corresponds to the first power receiving apparatus, after the first identification information is obtained; and 
 wirelessly perform power transfer to the second power receiving apparatus via a second coil which is included in the plurality of coils and which corresponds to the second power receiving apparatus, after the second identification information is obtained, 
   wherein the unit performs control such that the process of the Ping is not executed via a coil adjacent to the first coil during the power transfer to the first power receiving apparatus via the first coil.   


         2 . The power transmission apparatus according to  claim 1 , wherein the Ping is an Analog Ping, and the process of the Ping comprises outputting the Analog Ping. 


         3 . The power transmission apparatus according to  claim 1 , wherein the Ping is a Digital Ping, and the process of the Ping comprises transmitting the Digital Ping. 


         4 . (canceled) 


         5 . A control method of a power transmission apparatus comprising a plurality of coils, the control method comprising:
 executing a process of a Ping;   obtaining, from a first power receiving apparatus, a first signal strength packet including a value related to a received power after the process of the Ping is executed for the first power receiving apparatus;   obtaining, from the first power receiving apparatus, first identification information of the first power receiving apparatus after the first signal strength packet is obtained;   obtaining, from a second power receiving apparatus, a second signal strength packet including a value related to a received power after the process of the Ping is executed for the second power receiving apparatus;   obtaining, from the second power receiving apparatus, second identification information of the second power receiving apparatus after the second signal strength packet is obtained;   wirelessly performing power transfer to the first power receiving apparatus via a first coil which is included in the plurality of coils and which corresponds to the first power receiving apparatus, after the first identification information is obtained; and   wirelessly performing power transfer to the second power receiving apparatus via a second coil which is included in the plurality of coils and which corresponds to the second power receiving apparatus, after the second identification information is obtained,   wherein the process of the Ping is controlled so that the process of the Ping is not executed via a coil adjacent to the first coil during the power transfer to the first power receiving apparatus via the first coil, and   wherein two or more coils among the plurality of coils are arranged along a first direction, and two or more coils among the plurality of coils are arranged along a second direction different from the first direction.   


         6 . (canceled)

