What is claimed is: 

         1 . A working platform for a surgical instrument counting system, comprising:
 a body portion;   a first placement portion connected to the body portion;   a second placement portion connected to the body portion;   a connecting device for connecting a plurality of first surgical instruments, each of the plurality of first surgical instruments having an annular portion; and   a surgical instrument carrier loaded with a plurality of second surgical instruments, none of the plurality of second surgical instruments having an annular portion;   wherein the connecting device is removably connected to the first placement portion, and/or the surgical instrument carrier is removably connected to the second placement portion.   


         2 . The working platform of  claim 1 , wherein the connecting device is a U-shaped rod. 


         3 . The working platform of  claim 1 , wherein the first placement portion comprises a movable portion and a groove portion, the movable portion can move along the groove portion;
 wherein the connecting device is removably connected to the movable portion of the first placement portion.   


         4 . A surgical instrument counting system, comprising:
 a computing device that captures a first image of a plurality of first surgical instruments to generate a first image data, the plurality of the first surgical instruments each having an annular portion;   wherein the computing device captures a second image of a plurality of second surgical instruments to generate a second image data, none of the plurality of second surgical instruments having an annular portion;   wherein the computing device generates a first counting data based on the first image data, the first counting data indicating a first number of the plurality of first surgical instruments;   wherein the computing device generates a second counting data based on the second image data, the second counting data indicating a second number of the plurality of second surgical instruments.   


         5 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 4 , wherein the computing device comprises an image capturing portion;
 wherein the surgical instrument counting system further comprises a connecting device connected to the annular portion of each of the plurality of first surgical instruments;   wherein, when the computing device captures the first image, the connecting device is disposed in front of the image capturing portion such that all of the plurality of first surgical instruments are positioned in front of the image capturing portion.   


         6 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 4 , further comprising: any working platform of  claims 1-3 , wherein the working platform comprises a third placement portion connected to the body portion, and the computing device is connected to the third placement portion;
 wherein the computing device captures the first image of the plurality of first surgical instruments on the connecting device when the connecting device is removably connected to the first placement portion, thereby generating the first image data;   wherein the computing device captures the second image of the plurality of second surgical instruments on the surgical instrument carrier when the surgical instrument carrier is removably connected to the second placement portion, thereby generating the second image data.   


         7 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 6 , wherein the computing device comprises an image capturing portion;
 wherein the first placement portion comprises a first positioning mechanism, which positions the connecting device in front of the image capturing portion when the connecting device is connected to the first placement portion.   


         8 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 6 , wherein the computing device comprises an image capturing portion;
 wherein the second placement portion comprises a second positioning mechanism, which positions the surgical instrument carrier in front of the image capturing portion when the surgical instrument carrier is connected to the second placement portion.   


         9 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 4 , wherein the computing device comprises a first deep-learning module;
 wherein the computing device receives a first training data, and the computing device uses the first training data to train the first deep-learning module such that the first deep-learning module can generate the first counting data based on the first image data.   


         10 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 4 , wherein the computing device comprises a second deep-learning module;
 wherein the computing device receives a second training data, and the computing device uses the second training data to train the second deep-learning module such that the second deep-learning module can generate the second counting data based on the second image data.   


         11 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 4 , wherein the plurality of first surgical instruments comprises a third surgical instrument having a first label portion;
 wherein the first image data comprises a first label image data indicating the image of the first label portion;   wherein the computing device generates a first identity data based on the first label image data, and the first identity data is indicative of at least one of the type, material, usage number, and usage history information of the third surgical instrument.   


         12 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 4 , wherein the plurality of second surgical instruments comprises a fourth surgical instrument having a second label portion;
 wherein the second image data includes a second label image data, which is indicative of the image of the second label portion;   wherein the computing device generates a second identity data based on the second label image data, wherein the second identity data is indicative of at least one of the type, material, usage number, and usage history information of the fourth surgical instrument.   


         13 . The surgical instrument counting system of  claim 4 , wherein the computing device comprises a display portion;
 wherein, when the computing device generates the first counting data based on the first image data, the display portion displays the first image data and/or the first counting data;   wherein, when the computing device generates the second counting data based on the second image data, the display portion displays the second image data and/or the second counting data.

