What is claimed is: 

         1 . An apparatus for wireless communication at a first device, comprising:
 memory; and   one or more processors coupled to the one or more memory and, based at least in part on information stored in the memory, the one or more processors are configured to:
 select a base graph (BG) from a plurality of BGs based on a set of configuration parameters associated with a scheduled low density parity check (LDPC) coded transmission; and 
 transmit the scheduled LDPC coded transmission to a second device, or receive the scheduled LDPC coded transmission from the second device, based on the selected BG. 



         2 . The apparatus of  claim 1 , wherein, to select the BG from the plurality of BGs based on the set of configuration parameters associated with the scheduled LDPC coded transmission, the one or more processors are configured to:
 select the BG based on a decoding complexity of the first device, wherein the decoding complexity comprises at least one of:
 a number of code blocks per transport block (TB); 
 a modulation and coding scheme (MCS); 
 a modulation order; 
 a number of layers; 
 a direction of communication being uplink, downlink, or sidelink; 
 a limited buffer rate matching being enabled for a TB; 
 a maximum number of multiple-output (MIMO) layers that are configured on a component carrier (CC); 
 a highest modulation order configured in the CC; 
 a first scheduled throughput of the CC; 
 a second scheduled throughput of a band; 
 a bandwidth of the scheduled LDPC coded transmission; or 
 any combination thereof. 



         3 . The apparatus of  claim 1 , wherein, to select the BG from the plurality of BGs based on the set of configuration parameters associated with the scheduled LDPC coded transmission, the one or more processors are configured to:
 select the BG based on a decoding complexity of the second device, wherein the decoding complexity comprises at least one of:
 a number of code blocks per transport block (TB); 
 a modulation and coding scheme (MCS); 
 a modulation order; 
 a number of layers; 
 a direction of communication being uplink, downlink, or sidelink; 
 a limited buffer rate matching being enabled for a TB; 
 a maximum number of multiple-output (MIMO) layers that are configured on a component carrier (CC); 
 a highest modulation order configured in the CC; 
 a first scheduled throughput of the CC; 
 a second scheduled throughput of a band; 
 a bandwidth of the scheduled LDPC coded transmission; or 
 any combination thereof. 



