What is claimed is: 

         1 . A punching machine with a replaceable punching core, comprising:
 a mounting base configured to carry a sheet material to be punched;   a replaceable punching core, which is detachably mounted on the mounting base, and the replaceable punching core comprises a punching assembly;   a control handle, which is rotatably connected to the mounting base and configured to drive the punching assembly of the replaceable punching core downward, thereby performing a punching operation on the sheet material carried on the mounting base.   


         2 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 1 , wherein the punching machine with the replaceable punching core further comprises an iron ring pressing assembly, the iron ring pressing assembly comprises a pressing fixed plate and a pressing movable plate; 
       wherein, when the control handle is rotated downward, the pressing movable plate moves toward the pressing fixed plate to press a binding iron ring located between the pressing fixed plate and the pressing movable plate; 
       wherein an initial position of the pressing fixed plate is adjustable to accommodate binding iron rings of different sizes. 


         3 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 2 , wherein the iron ring pressing assembly further comprises an adjusting control component and an adjusting execution component; 
       wherein the adjusting execution component is fixedly connected to the pressing fixed plate, the adjusting control component is slidably connected to the adjusting execution component; and the initial position of the pressing fixed plate is adjusted to move closer to or away from the pressing movable plate by operating the adjusting execution component. 


         4 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 3 , wherein the adjusting execution component is provided with a sliding groove, the adjusting control component is provided with a sliding rod; 
       wherein the sliding rod is slidably received in the sliding groove, and the position of the adjusting execution component is adjusted by adjusting a position of the sliding rod relative to the sliding groove, thereby moving the initial position of the pressing fixed plate to move closer to or away from the pressing movable plate. 


         5 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 4 , wherein the adjusting control component is provided with a control portion, the mounting base further comprises a through slot, and the control portion extends out of and is slidably connected to the through slot. 


         6 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 2 , wherein the mounting base is provided with a handle installing shaft, the control handle is provided with a handle installing hole that cooperates with the handle installing shaft; the mounting base and the control handle are rotatably connected through the handle installing shaft. 


         7 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 6 , wherein the punching machine with the replaceable punching core further comprises an elastic reset assembly sleeved on the handle installing shaft; and the elastic reset assembly is configured to drive the control handle to automatically return to an initial position after the punching operation is completed. 


         8 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 7 , wherein the elastic reset assembly comprises an elastic component and an abutting rod; the abutting rod is fixedly connected to the mounting base, and the elastic component is sleeved on the handle installing shaft and configured to abut against the abutting rod. 


         9 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 7 , wherein the punching machine with the replaceable punching core further comprises a driving gear and a transmission assembly; 
       the driving gear is fixedly sleeved on the handle installing shaft and provided with a first gear portion, the transmission assembly is vertically and slidably connected to the mounting base; and the transmission assembly is provided with a transmission engaging hole that meshes with the first gear portion. 


         10 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 9 , wherein, when the control handle is rotated downward, the driving gear rotates accordingly and drives the transmission assembly to move downward through a mesh engagement between the first gear portion and the transmission engaging hole. 


         11 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 10 , wherein the transmission assembly further comprises an executing plate, the executing plate is provided with an executing slot; the punching assembly comprises a punching pressure plate and a punching blade; 
       wherein the executing slot clamps the punching pressure plate, and the punching pressure plate abuts against the punching blade; 
       when the transmission assembly moves downward, the executing plate is driven to move downward, and then the punching blade is driven to move downward through the punching pressure plate clamped in the executing slot, so as to punch the sheet material carried on the mounting base. 


         12 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 11 , wherein the punching machine with the replaceable punching core further comprises a limiting assembly, the limiting assembly is configured to lock the control handle at the lowest position of a swing stroke. 


         13 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 12 , wherein the limiting assembly comprises a limiting plate and a control card; 
       the limiting plate is fixedly connected to the executing plate so as to move together with the movement of the executing plate; and the limiting plate is provided with a locking portion. 


         14 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 13 , wherein the control card is slidably connected to the mounting base and is provided with a control abutment portion; 
       wherein, when the control handle reaches the lowest position of the swing stroke, the control abutment portion abuts against the locking portion. 


         15 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 14 , wherein, when the control abutment portion abuts against the locking portion, the limiting assembly locks the control handle against an elastic force of the elastic reset assembly. 


         16 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 1 , wherein the punching machine with the replaceable punching core further comprises a base positioning assembly, the base positioning assembly is disposed on the mounting base and configured to transversely adjust a position of the sheet material to be punched. 


         17 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 1 , wherein the mounting base is provided with a mounting sink slot, and an outer contour of the bottom of the replaceable punching core matches the mounting sink slot. 


         18 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 9 , wherein the iron ring pressing assembly further comprises a joining component, the joining component is fixedly connected to the pressing movable plate. 


         19 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 18 , wherein the joining component is provided with a pressing engaging hole, the driving gear is further provided with a second gear portion; 
       wherein, when the control handle is rotated downward, the driving gear drives the joining component through a mesh engagement between the second gear portion and the pressing engaging hole, thereby driving the pressing movable plate move toward the pressing fixed plate to press the binding iron ring located between the pressing fixed plate and the pressing movable plate. 


         20 . The punching machine with the replaceable punching core of  claim 2 , wherein the mounting base further comprises an iron ring installing portion; 
       wherein the iron ring installing portion is disposed correspondingly to the iron ring pressing assembly and configured to assist in mounting the binding iron ring onto the sheet material on which the punching operation has been completed, before the iron ring pressing assembly presses the binding iron ring.

What is claimed is: 

         1 . A remote-controlled lighting system, comprising: a remote controller, at least one lighting fixture, and a controller configured for each lighting fixture;
 the controller comprises a main control unit, a dip switch component connected to the main control unit, and a wireless communication unit; the dip switch component comprises a plurality of gear switches for setting unique identity identifier for a corresponding lighting fixture;   the remote control is wirelessly connected to the wireless communication unit and is provided with control buttons and a plurality of gear selection buttons corresponding to the number of the gear switches; each of the gear selection buttons is configured to send a target gear remote control command carrying a corresponding button identifier to the main control unit;   when the button identifier in a received target gear remote control command matches a current identity identifier of the corresponding lighting fixture, the main control unit responds to the control command of the control button to drive the corresponding lighting fixture to perform a corresponding lighting action; otherwise, it does not respond to the control command of the control button.   


         2 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 1 , wherein the type of the identity identifier is any one of numbers, letters, combinations of numbers and letters, and special symbols, and the type of button identifier is any one of numbers, letters, combinations of numbers and letters, and special symbols, with each button identifier matching a unique identity identifier. 


         3 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 2 , wherein the dip switch component comprises N gear switches, which are respectively corresponded to 1 to N numeric identity identifiers for the corresponding lighting fixture;
 the gear selection buttons of the remote control are configured to be 1 to N numerical buttons, and the N numerical buttons correspond to the 1 to N button identifiers;   the 1 to N button identifiers are matched one-to-one with the 1 to N numeric identity identifiers, where N is a natural number and N≥2.   


         4 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 3 , wherein the main control unit comprises a main control chip U 1  and a capacitor C 1 ;
 a 4 th  pin of the main control chip U 1  is used to connect to a working voltage of 3.3V, an 11 th  pin of the main control chip U 1  is grounded, one end of the capacitor C 1  is connected to the 4 th  pin of the main control chip U 1 , and the other end is grounded; 
 the main control chip U 1  also has N pins connected to the N gear switches one by one. 



         5 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 4 , wherein the main control unit further comprises an interface P 2 , and the wireless communication unit is connected to a 12 th  pin of the main control chip U 1  through a 3 rd  pin of the interface P 2 . 


         6 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 4 , wherein the main control unit further comprises an interface P 1 , a resistor R 7 , a resistor R 8 , a resistor R 9 , a resistor R 10 , a resistor R 11 , a resistor R 12 , a MOS transistor Q 1 , and a MOS transistor Q 2 ;
 the interface P 1  is connected to the lighting fixture, a collector electrode of the MOS transistor Q 1  is connected to a 2 nd  pin of the interface P 1  through the resistor R 7 , a collector electrode of the MOS transistor Q 2  is connected to a 3 rd  pin of the interface P 1  through the resistor R 8 , a source electrode of the MOS transistor Q 1  is grounded, the resistor R 11  is connected between a gate electrode and a source electrode of the MOS transistor Q 1 , a 13rd pin of the main control chip U 1  is connected to a gate electrode of the MOS transistor Q 1  through the resistor R 9 , a source electrode of the MOS transistor Q 2  is grounded, the resistor R 12  is connected between a gate electrode and a source electrode of the MOS transistor Q 12 , and a 14 th  pin of the main control chip U 1  is connected to a gate electrode of the MOS transistor Q 2  through the resistor R 10 .   


         7 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 1 , wherein the control buttons comprise a main switch button, a lamp switch button, a brightness adjustment button, and a color temperature adjustment button, and the lighting action comprises turning on and off the lamp, adjusting the brightness, and adjusting the color temperature. 


         8 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 1 , wherein the wireless communication unit is a 2.4G wireless communication unit. 


         9 . The remote-controlled lighting system according to  claim 1 , wherein the dip switch component is a dip switch.

