         21 . A detection system for determining an operational state of a well in a completion operation, the system comprising a processor configured to:
 receive set of well operations data, the received data comprising at least some measured well operations data;   determine the occurrence of a well operations event based on the received data;   after determining the occurrence of the event, evaluate one or more possible state transitions from a current well operations state to one or more possible new well operations states, the current state and the possible new states selected from a configurable plurality of well operations states, wherein, evaluating the one or more possible state transitions is based on the current state, the determined event and the received data and wherein, to evaluate the one or more possible state transitions, the processor is configured to determine a confidence level associated with each of the possible new states; and   determine one of the possible new states to be a new predicted well operations state according to whichever possible new state has a highest confidence level.   


         22 . The system of  claim 21  wherein, to evaluate the one or more possible state transitions, the processor is configured to select the one or more possible new states from among the plurality of well operations states based on the current state. 


         23 . The system of  claim 21  comprising one or more valve position sensors, each valve position sensor measuring a position of a corresponding valve and wherein, to receive the set of data, the processor is configured to receive measured valve position data from the one or more valve position sensors. 


         24 . The system of  claim 23  wherein, to determine the occurrence of the event based on the received data, the processor is configured to determine from at least one of the one or more valve position sensors that its corresponding valve has transitioned from open to closed or from closed to open. 


         25 . The system of  claim 23  wherein the one or more valve positions sensors comprise a plurality of valve position sensors and wherein, to determine the occurrence of the event based on the received data, the processor is configured to determining from a group of two or more of the plurality of valve position sensors that their corresponding valves have transitioned from open to closed or from closed to open. 


         26 . The system of  claim 23  wherein, to determine the occurrence of the event based on the received data, the processor is configured to determine from at least one of the one or more valve position sensors that its corresponding valve is being greased. 


         27 . The system of  claim 23  wherein the processor is configured to evaluate the one or more possible state transitions from the current state to the one or more possible new states based at least in part on the measured valve position data. 


         28 . The system of  claim 23  wherein the processor is configured to determine the confidence level associated with each of the possible new states based at least in part on the measured valve position data. 


         29 . The system of  claim 23  comprising one or more pressure sensors, each pressure sensor measuring pressure in a corresponding region of the well and wherein, to receive the set of data, the processor is configured to receive measured pressure data from the one or more pressure sensors. 


         30 . The system of  claim 29  wherein, to determine the occurrence of the event based on the received data, the processor is configured to determine that the pressure measured by at least one of the one or more pressure sensors has crossed from above a configurable threshold to below the configurable threshold or from below the configurable threshold to above the configurable threshold. 


         31 . The system of  claim 29  wherein the processor is configured to evaluate the one or more possible state transitions from the current state to the one or more possible new states based at least in part on the measured pressure data. 


