What is claimed is: 

         1 . A system comprising:
 circuitry configured to:
 acquire, via a communication interface coupled to a packet-switched network, an audio signal from an acoustic sensor, convert the audio signal into a digital signal, and store the digital signal in a memory; 
 segment the digital signal into time-domain and frequency-domain frames, perform short-time spectral analysis on the frames, identify a noise component and a speech component based on the analysis, and generate a processed speech signal in which the noise component is suppressed and the speech component is emphasized; 
 detect a speech section in the processed speech signal, perform speech recognition processing on the speech section, extract a keyword based on a stored keyword group, and identify the speech section including the keyword; 
 convert the identified speech section into a vibration signal and output the vibration signal to an actuator; 
 calculate a position of a user based on at least one of a satellite positioning signal, a wireless communication signal, or an output of an inertial sensor, and generate position history data; 
 determine a position state of the user based on the position history data and wireless environment data, and generate region data corresponding to the determined position state; 
 acquire environment data and service data from an external information source via the packet-switched network based on the region data; 
 calculate a relevance value for each acquired data item based on the position history data, the extracted keyword, and use history data of the user, rank the acquired data items according to the relevance value, and select presentation target data; 
 convert the presentation target data into audio output data and generate combined audio data by mixing the audio output data with the processed speech signal for output via the actuator; and 
 construct an input prompt comprising the position state, the extracted keyword, and the acquired data, transmit the input prompt to a generative language model, receive a response, and update at least one of the audio output data or a ranking condition based on the response. 



         2 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to calculate a movement speed and a movement direction of the user based on the satellite positioning signal, the wireless communication signal, and the output of the inertial sensor, and to include the movement speed and the movement direction in the position history data. 


         3 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to determine the position state as an indoor position state or an outdoor position state based on the position history data and a signal strength of the wireless communication signal, and to generate the region data comprising at least one of a floor identifier or an area identifier for the indoor position state. 


         4 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to perform the short-time spectral analysis by applying a window function to each frame, computing a short-time Fourier transform to obtain a complex spectrum, estimating a noise power spectrum, and suppressing the noise component by attenuating the noise power spectrum from the complex spectrum in each frequency bin. 


         5 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to compute, for each frame of the digital signal, mel-frequency cepstral coefficients, log-mel filterbank energies, frame energy, spectral centroid, and fundamental frequency, and to concatenate per-frame feature vectors into a time-series feature array for use in at least one of the speech recognition processing or an emotion estimation model. 


         6 . The system according to  claim 5 , wherein the circuitry is configured to input the time-series feature array into an emotion estimation neural network comprising at least one recurrent or attention-based layer, compute scores for a plurality of predefined emotion categories, apply a softmax function to the scores, and select an emotion label based on a maximum probability. 


         7 . The system according to  claim 6 , wherein the circuitry is configured to adjust at least one of a volume level, a speaking speed, or a notification frequency of the audio output data based on the emotion label and the scores. 


         8 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to calculate the relevance value by computing a proximity score, an urgency score, an emotion-adjusted relevance score, and a preference match score for each acquired data item, and combining the scores using a weighted sum or a non-linear function to produce a presentation priority value. 


         9 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the environment data comprises at least one of weather data, transportation data, or facility data, and the service data comprises at least one of promotional data or event data associated with the region data. 


         10 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to invoke a text-to-speech engine to synthesize an audio waveform from the presentation target data, adjust an amplitude and a dynamic range of the audio waveform based on user hearing preference data, and convert the audio waveform into the vibration signal via a digital-to-analog converter for output to the actuator. 


         11 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the actuator comprises a bone-conduction actuator configured to produce mechanical vibrations that propagate through bone to an inner ear of the user. 


         12 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the input prompt comprises a natural language description of the position state, the emotion label, a current notification rule configuration, and an optimization goal, and wherein the response from the generative language model comprises at least one of updated scoring weights, category priorities, notification rate parameters, or message template data. 


         13 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to suppress the presentation target data having a priority below a threshold when an emotion-derived stress index of the user exceeds a predetermined stress threshold. 


         14 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to scan a plurality of wireless access point signals receivable at the position of the user, compute a signal strength vector from the scanned signals, compare the signal strength vector with stored reference signal strength vectors associated with known regions, and determine the region data based on a closest matching reference signal strength vector. 


         15 . The system according to  claim 2 , wherein the circuitry is configured to determine, based on the movement speed and the movement direction in the position history data, a movement context of the user as one of a stationary state, a walking state, or a vehicular state, and to suppress presentation of the presentation target data requiring visual attention when the movement context corresponds to the vehicular state. 


         16 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to perform the speech recognition processing by computing, frame by frame, a probability distribution over phonetic units using a neural acoustic model, and performing decoding with a beam search algorithm to obtain a text sequence. 


         17 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is configured to transmit, to a server via the packet-switched network, state data comprising the position history data, the extracted keyword, and emotion data, and to receive, from the server, the presentation target data selected based on the state data. 


         18 . A system comprising:
 circuitry configured to:
 acquire, via a communication interface coupled to a packet-switched network, an audio signal from an acoustic sensor, convert the audio signal into a digital signal, segment the digital signal into frames, apply a window function to each frame, and compute a short-time Fourier transform to obtain a complex spectrum; 
 estimate a noise power spectrum from the complex spectrum, suppress a noise component by attenuating the noise power spectrum in each frequency bin, and generate a processed speech signal in which the noise component is suppressed and a speech component is emphasized; 
 compute, for each frame, mel-frequency cepstral coefficients, log-mel filterbank energies, frame energy, spectral centroid, and fundamental frequency, and concatenate per-frame feature vectors into a time-series feature array; 
 perform speech recognition processing on the processed speech signal using a neural acoustic model to compute a probability distribution over phonetic units and a beam search decoder to obtain a text sequence, extract a keyword based on a stored keyword group, and identify a speech section including the keyword; 
 convert the identified speech section into a vibration signal and output the vibration signal to a bone-conduction actuator configured to produce mechanical vibrations that propagate through bone to an inner ear of a user; 
 calculate a position of the user based on at least one of a satellite positioning signal, a wireless communication signal, or an output of an inertial sensor, determine a position state, and acquire environment data and service data from an external information source via the packet-switched network based on the position state; 
 calculate a relevance value for each acquired data item by computing a proximity score, an urgency score, an emotion-adjusted relevance score, and a preference match score and combining the scores to produce a presentation priority value, and select presentation target data based on the presentation priority value; 
 input the time-series feature array into an emotion estimation neural network comprising at least one recurrent or attention-based layer, compute scores for a plurality of predefined emotion categories, and select an emotion label; 
 generate combined audio data by mixing audio output data derived from the presentation target data with the processed speech signal for output via the bone-conduction actuator, and adjust at least one of a volume level, a speaking speed, or a notification frequency of the audio output data based on the emotion label; and 
 construct an input prompt comprising the position state, the extracted keyword, the emotion label, and the acquired data, transmit the input prompt to a generative language model, receive a response, and update at least one of the audio output data or a ranking condition based on the response. 



         19 . The system according to  claim 18 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to suppress the presentation target data having a priority below a threshold when an emotion-derived stress index of the user exceeds a predetermined stress threshold. 


         20 . A method performed by circuitry of a system, the method comprising:
 acquiring, via a communication interface coupled to a packet-switched network, an audio signal from an acoustic sensor, converting the audio signal into a digital signal, and storing the digital signal in a memory;   segmenting the digital signal into time-domain and frequency-domain frames, performing short-time spectral analysis, and generating a processed speech signal in which a noise component is suppressed and a speech component is emphasized;   detecting a speech section in the processed speech signal, performing speech recognition processing, extracting a keyword based on a stored keyword group, and identifying the speech section including the keyword;   converting the identified speech section into a vibration signal and outputting the vibration signal to an actuator;   calculating a position of a user, generating position history data, determining a position state, and acquiring environment data and service data from an external information source via the packet-switched network based on the position state;   calculating a relevance value for each acquired data item, ranking and selecting presentation target data, and generating combined audio data by mixing audio output data with the processed speech signal; and   constructing an input prompt comprising the position state, the extracted keyword, and the acquired data, transmitting the input prompt to a generative language model, receiving a response, and updating at least one of the audio output data or a ranking condition based on the response.

