What is claimed is: 

         1 . A method comprising:
 receiving, by data processing hardware, a time series anomaly detection query from a user, the time series anomaly detection query comprising a user-specified anomaly probability and requesting the data processing hardware to determine one or more anomalies in a set of time series data values;   training, by the data processing hardware, a chain of two or more models using each time series data value in the set of time series data values, wherein the two or more models includes a separate model for each component from a plurality of components to improve scalability; and   for each respective time series data value in the set of time series data values:
 determining, by the data processing hardware and using the chain of two or more models, an expected data value for the respective time series data value; 
 determining, by the data processing hardware, an interval size based on the user-specified anomaly probability; 
 determining, by the data processing hardware, an upper bound and a lower bound based on the expected data value and the interval size; 
 determining, by the data processing hardware, whether the respective time series data value is greater than the upper bound or less than the lower bound; 
 in response to determining that the respective time series data value is greater than the upper bound or less than the lower bound, determining, by the data processing hardware, that the respective time series data value is anomalous; and 
 reporting, by the data processing hardware, the respective time series data value to the user. 



         2 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the user-specified anomaly probability configures a rate of false positives for the one or more anomalies. 


         3 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein determining the interval size is further based on a standard error from the chain of two or more models. 


         4 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein determining the expected data value for the respective time series data value comprises decomposing each time series data value in the set of time series data values into a plurality of components. 


         5 . The method of  claim 4 , wherein the plurality of components comprises one or more of a trend component, a holiday effect component, a seasonal component, and a step change component. 


         6 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein reporting the respective time series data value further comprises reporting data regarding a relative difference between the expected data value and the respective time series data value. 


         7 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the respective time series data value comprises a future time series data value that the one or more models do not train on. 


         8 . A system comprising:
 data processing hardware; and   memory hardware in communication with the data processing hardware, the memory hardware storing instructions that when executed on the data processing hardware cause the data processing hardware to:
 receive a time series anomaly detection query from a user, the time series anomaly detection query comprising a user-specified anomaly probability and requesting the data processing hardware to determine one or more anomalies in a set of time series data values; 
 train a chain of two or more models using each time series data value in the set of time series data values, wherein the two or more models includes a separate model for each component from a plurality of components to improve scalability; and 
 for each respective time series data value in the set of time series data values:
 determine, using the chain of two or more models, an expected data value for the respective time series data value; 
 determine an interval size based on the user-specified anomaly probability; 
 determine an upper bound and a lower bound based on the expected data value and the interval size; 
 determine whether the respective time series data value is greater than the upper bound or less than the lower bound; 
 in response to determining that the respective time series data value is greater than the upper bound or less than the lower bound, determine that the respective time series data value is anomalous; and 
 report the respective time series data value to the user. 




         9 . The system of  claim 8 , wherein the user-specified anomaly probability configures a rate of false positives for the one or more anomalies. 


         10 . The system of  claim 8 , wherein the instructions further cause the data processing hardware to determine the interval size based on a standard error from the chain of two or more models. 


         11 . The system of  claim 8 , wherein the instructions that cause the data processing hardware to determine the expected data value for the respective time series data value further cause the data processing hardware to decompose each time series data value in the set of time series data values into a plurality of components. 


         12 . The system of  claim 11 , wherein the plurality of components comprises one or more of a trend component, a holiday effect component, a seasonal component, and a step change component. 


         13 . The system of  claim 8 , wherein the instructions that cause the data processing hardware to report the respective time series data value further cause the data processing hardware to report data regarding a relative difference between the expected data value and the respective time series data value. 


         14 . The system of  claim 8 , wherein the respective time series data value comprises a future time series data value that the one or more models do not train on. 


