What is claimed is: 

         1 . A computer-implemented method using a computing system to validate and publish non-fungible token (NFT) content with tamper-evident provenance on an object distributed ledger, the method comprising:
 receiving, by a computing device of the computing system comprising a blockchain node with a peer-to-peer networking interface, a consensus module implementing an append-only blockchain with a Merkle-tree state, and a cryptographic engine of a processing module, from a digital record of baseline content of an evaluation request from a user device of the computing system, and extracting from the digital record a contingency entity identifier (ID), an outcome provider ID, a value of a result of a triggered outcome, obligation requirements, an obligation provider identifier (ID), an outcome recipient ID, and an obligation recipient ID, wherein the obligation provider ID is associated with providing of an obligation tied to the obligation recipient ID in accordance with the obligation requirements, wherein the outcome recipient ID is associated with the result of the triggered outcome tied to the outcome provider ID in accordance with contingent outcome rules and an obligation status, wherein a positive obligation status indicates that the obligation has historically been provided in accordance with the obligation requirements;   identifying, by the computing device, an accreditation authority computing device of the computing system by consulting a registry that maps the obligation recipient ID to an accreditation authority identifier and corresponding public key material;   obtaining, by the computing device, baseline validation information from the accreditation authority computing device, the baseline validation information comprising a digital signature over a canonicalized digest of the baseline content and a validation timestamp;   validating, by the cryptographic engine, the baseline content by:
 recomputing the canonicalized digest of the baseline content, 
 verifying the digital signature using a public key bound to the accreditation authority, 
 confirming that the accreditation authority is not revoked according to a revocation status indicator, and 
 indicating the baseline content is valid when the validation succeeds; 
   establishing, by the computing device, non-fungible token (NFT) content including the baseline content, an availability status, and an accreditation authority signature reference to produce an NFT;   synchronizing, by the computing device, with the object distributed ledger to a finalized block height having at least a threshold number of confirmations;   computing, by the cryptographic engine, a transaction digest over a canonical representation of the NFT content together with a nonce, a chain identifier, and a previous block hash, encrypting at least a portion of the NFT content using a receiving public key associated with the object distributed and generating a transaction signature by signing the transaction digest with a private key of the computing device;   causing, by the consensus module, generation of a next block of a blockchain of the object distributed ledger including the NFT content, the encrypted portion, a Merkle root committing the NFT content, and the transaction signature; and   causing, by the computing device, inclusion of the next block as a new block in the object distributed ledger and recording a Merkle proof of inclusion for the NFT content, wherein inclusion of the chain identifier, the previous block hash, and the nonce in the transaction digest prevents replay across ledgers or epochs, the recorded Merkle proof provides tamper-evident provenance, and the threshold number of confirmations provides finalized custody within a bounded time window.   


