 a peer-to-peer networking interface;   a local memory; and   a processing module operably coupled to the peer-to-peer networking interface and the local memory, wherein the processing module includes a cryptographic engine and a consensus module that implements an append-only blockchain with a Merkle-tree state, the processing module functions to:
 receive, via the peer-to-peer networking interface, from a digital record of baseline content of an evaluation request from a user device of the computing system, and extract from the digital record a contingency entity identifier (ID), an outcome provider ID, a value of a result of a triggered outcome, obligation requirements, an obligation provider identifier (ID), an outcome recipient ID, and an obligation recipient ID, wherein the obligation provider ID is associated with providing of an obligation tied to the obligation recipient ID in accordance with the obligation requirements, wherein the outcome recipient ID is associated with the result of the triggered outcome tied to the outcome provider ID in accordance with contingent outcome rules and an obligation status, wherein a positive obligation status indicates that the obligation has historically been provided in accordance with the obligation requirements; 
 identify an accreditation authority computing device of the computing system by consulting a registry that maps the obligation recipient ID to an accreditation authority identifier and corresponding public key material; 
 obtain, via the peer-to-peer networking interface, baseline validation information from the accreditation authority computing device, the baseline validation information comprising a digital signature over a canonicalized digest of the baseline content and a validation timestamp; 
 validate, by the cryptographic engine, the baseline content by:
 recomputing the canonicalized digest of the baseline content, 
 verifying the digital signature using a public key bound to the accreditation authority, 
