We claim: 

         1 . A system for generating key vocabulary phrases, comprising:
 a. a processor, wherein the processor is configured to perform an operation that generate phrases, the operation comprising:
 i. receiving a user-specified term or phrases that involves text cleaning; 
 ii. deriving a knowledge graph using the relationship of plurality of key phrases, thereby deriving a lemma; 
 iii. improving the quality of the key phrases using the transformer models; 
 iv. storing phrases, document ids and statistical details about phrases such as frequency, TF-IDF in a knowledge graph database; 
 v. ordering the phrases identified using the ranking criteria based on the phrases statistics; 
 vi. selecting and returning best key phrases as search results; and 
 vii. showing the search results as word cloud for the users to quickly identify the key vocabulary. 



         2 . A non-transitory computer-readable storage medium storing instructions that, when executed by a processor, cause a computer system to generate phrases, by performing the steps of:
 i. receiving a user-specified term or phrases that involves text cleaning;   ii. deriving a knowledge graph using the relationship of plurality of key phrases, thereby deriving a lemma;   iii. improving the quality of the key phrases using the transformer models;   iv. storing phrases, document ids and statistical details about phrases such as frequency, TF-IDF in a knowledge graph database;   v. ordering the phrases identified using the ranking criteria based on the phrases statistics;   vi. selecting and returning best key phrases as search results; and   vii. showing the search results as word cloud for the users to quickly identify the key vocabulary.   


         3 . A computer-implemented method ( 100 ) for generating key vocabulary phrases, the method comprising the steps of:
 receiving ( 101 ) a user-specified term or phrases by means of typing text or voice input and involves in text cleaning ( 101 A), wherein the means of typing text or voice input denotes the mode of input through input devices such as keyboard, touchscreen, microphone and other such devices to the method ( 100 ) for generating vocabulary phases;   identifying ( 102 ) domain specific vocabulary;   extracting ( 103 ) relationship between plurality of key phrases in a text document;   deriving ( 104 ,  104 A- 104 D) a knowledge graph using the relationship of plurality of key phrases, wherein each key phrase is a node in the knowledge graph and the relationship between two phrases establish a connection to form edge relationship in the knowledge graph, thereby deriving a lemma;   improving ( 105 ) the quality of the key phrases using the transformer models;   storing ( 106 ) phrases, document ids and statistical details about phrases such as frequency, TF-IDF in a knowledge graph database;   ordering ( 107 ) the phrases identified using the ranking criteria based on the phrases statistics;   selecting ( 108 ) and returning best key phrases as search results;   characterized by that,   the text cleaning ( 101 A) step comprising:
 extracting user specified text from the documents using approaches such as image to text, HTML parsing, PDF parsing and other such approaches; 
 preprocessing the extracted text from documents to eliminate different types of noises in the text, wherein the preprocessing step extracted text involving noise removal comprises of noises such as mathematical equations, figures, pictures, flowcharts, tables, non-english text, HTML links and other such noises; 
 extracting the text along with relevant meta data details using libraries, wherein the step of extracting text involves in removal of wrong hyphenation, incorrect fusing of two or more words, and spelling mistakes; 
   and showing ( 109 ) the search results as word cloud for the users to quickly identify the key vocabulary.   


         4 . The method as claimed in  claim 3 , wherein the improving ( 105 ) step of the quality of the key phrases uses BERT variants.

