What is claimed is: 

         1 . A system comprising:
 circuitry configured to:
 acquire, via a plurality of communication interfaces operating over a packet-switched network, data records from a plurality of heterogeneous information exchange services; 
 perform natural language processing on text data of each data record, the natural language processing comprising tokenization, extraction of feature terms based on term frequency-inverse document frequency computation, and detection of rule-based keyword features; 
 generate, for each data record, structured analysis input data comprising the feature terms and hint information derived from the rule-based keyword features; 
 transmit, to a generative artificial intelligence model, input information comprising the structured analysis input data together with a prompt sentence that specifies an output format for at least an urgency classification, an importance classification, and one or more extracted keywords; 
 receive, from the generative artificial intelligence model, response information comprising the urgency classification, the importance classification, and the one or more extracted keywords; 
 convert the urgency classification and the importance classification into numerical scores and integrate the numerical scores with output of a classification model that is trained using operation history data; 
 allocate each data record to one of a plurality of priority queues based on the integrated numerical scores; and 
 generate, for data records allocated to a first priority queue, output data comprising a condensed text representation produced by the generative artificial intelligence model in accordance with a task-specific prompt sentence, and transmit the output data to a client terminal via the packet-switched network. 



         2 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the plurality of heterogeneous information exchange services comprise at least an electronic mail service, an interactive text-based communication service, and a business management service. 


         3 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to acquire the data records by connecting to the electronic mail service using an internet message access protocol, connecting to the interactive text-based communication service using a request-response protocol over a secure transport layer, and connecting to a real-time communication service using a bidirectional persistent-connection protocol. 


         4 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to perform text normalization on the text data of each data record prior to the tokenization, the text normalization comprising decoding character encodings into a standardized encoding, removing markup elements, and deleting redundant thread content using pattern-based rules. 


         5 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the structured analysis input data further comprises attribute information of each data record, the attribute information including at least a sender category, a data record length, a number of recipients, and a historical interaction metric associated with a sender. 


         6 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the prompt sentence transmitted to the generative artificial intelligence model further includes one or more example data records with associated classification labels as few-shot examples to guide the urgency classification and the importance classification. 


         7 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the classification model comprises a gradient boosting decision tree model trained on feature vectors derived from the feature terms, sender attributes, and the rule-based keyword features, with labels representing urgency and importance levels determined from the operation history data. 


         8 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the classification model comprises a neural network classifier having a multi-layer perceptron with rectified linear activation functions, the neural network classifier being trained to output urgency scores and importance scores. 


         9 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to update parameters of the classification model by performing gradient-based optimization on batches of training examples derived from the operation history data, the gradient-based optimization comprising an adaptive moment estimation algorithm. 


         10 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to modify contents of the prompt sentence based on patterns identified in the operation history data, the modification comprising adding contextual instructions that reflect user-specific classification preferences associated with particular senders. 


         11 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the plurality of priority queues comprise a high-priority queue, a normal-priority queue, and a low-priority queue, and wherein the circuitry allocates each data record to one of the high-priority queue, the normal-priority queue, and the low-priority queue by comparing the integrated numerical scores against configurable threshold values. 


         12 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the task-specific prompt sentence for generating the condensed text representation specifies a maximum character count and instructs the generative artificial intelligence model to highlight a main issue and urgency of the data record. 


         13 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to group data records allocated to a second priority queue according to time-based or category-based conditions, to transmit to the generative artificial intelligence model a summarization-oriented prompt sentence that specifies extraction of decision information, issue information, and deadline information, and to store summary information received from the generative artificial intelligence model in association with the grouped data records. 


         14 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to receive, from the client terminal, feedback data indicating at least one of an opening operation, an ignoring operation, a priority change operation, and a setting change operation, and to record the feedback data as the operation history data for updating the classification model. 


         15 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the generative artificial intelligence model comprises a transformer-based neural network having a plurality of self-attention layers and feed-forward sublayers with learned parameters. 


         16 . The system according to  claim 1 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to estimate an emotional state of a user associated with the client terminal by computing feature values from notification history and operation history received from the client terminal, inputting the feature values to a machine learning model trained to classify emotional states, and adjusting a composite priority calculation for each data record based on the estimated emotional state. 


         17 . The system according to  claim 16 , wherein the feature values comprise at least an average notification opening delay, a non-opening rate, a quick deletion rate, and a frequency of setting a do-not-disturb mode, and wherein the machine learning model comprises a feed-forward neural network with a softmax output layer that outputs probability scores for emotional state labels. 


         18 . A system comprising:
 circuitry configured to:
 acquire, via a plurality of communication interfaces operating over a packet-switched network using at least an internet message access protocol, a request-response protocol over a secure transport layer, and a bidirectional persistent-connection protocol, data records from a plurality of heterogeneous information exchange services, and convert the data records into a normalized common format; 
 perform text normalization on text data of each data record by decoding character encodings into a standardized encoding, removing markup elements using a parser, and deleting redundant thread content using pattern-based rules; 
 tokenize the normalized text data using a language-specific tokenizer to produce token sequences with associated morphological information and part-of-speech information; 
 compute term frequency-inverse document frequency values for each token across a sliding window of data records, select feature terms having term frequency-inverse document frequency values exceeding a predetermined threshold, and detect rule-based keyword features by evaluating regular expression patterns against the token sequences to identify urgency-related terms and deadline-related terms; 
 generate, for each data record, structured analysis input data comprising attribute information, the feature terms, and hint information derived from the rule-based keyword features; 
 transmit, to a generative artificial intelligence model comprising a transformer-based neural network having a plurality of self-attention layers and feed-forward sublayers, input information comprising the structured analysis input data together with a prompt sentence that specifies an output format for at least an urgency classification, an importance classification, and one or more extracted keywords, the prompt sentence further including one or more example data records with associated classification labels; 
 receive, from the generative artificial intelligence model, response information, and parse the response information using deterministic parsing rules to extract the urgency classification, the importance classification, and the one or more extracted keywords; 
 convert the urgency classification and the importance classification into numerical scores, input feature vectors derived from the feature terms and sender attributes into a classification model trained using operation history data, and integrate the numerical scores from the generative artificial intelligence model with output scores from the classification model using a weighted aggregation rule; 
 allocate each data record to one of a high-priority queue, a normal-priority queue, and a low-priority queue based on the integrated scores and configurable threshold values; 
 generate, for data records allocated to the high-priority queue, output data comprising a condensed text representation produced by the generative artificial intelligence model in accordance with a notification-specific prompt sentence that specifies a maximum character count, and transmit the output data to a client terminal via the packet-switched network; and 
 group data records allocated to the low-priority queue according to time-based or category-based conditions, transmit to the generative artificial intelligence model a summarization-oriented prompt sentence that specifies extraction of decision information, issue information, and deadline information, and store summary information received from the generative artificial intelligence model for subsequent retrieval by the client terminal. 



         19 . The system according to  claim 18 , wherein the circuitry is further configured to modify contents of the prompt sentence dynamically based on patterns identified in operation history data received from the client terminal, the modification comprising adding contextual instructions that reflect user-specific classification preferences associated with particular senders, and to periodically retrain the classification model by performing gradient-based optimization on training examples derived from the operation history data. 


         20 . A method performed by circuitry of a system, the method comprising:
 acquiring, via a plurality of communication interfaces operating over a packet-switched network, data records from a plurality of heterogeneous information exchange services;   performing natural language processing on text data of each data record, the natural language processing comprising tokenization, extraction of feature terms based on term frequency-inverse document frequency computation, and detection of rule-based keyword features;   generating, for each data record, structured analysis input data comprising the feature terms and hint information derived from the rule-based keyword features;   transmitting, to a generative artificial intelligence model, input information comprising the structured analysis input data together with a prompt sentence that specifies an output format for at least an urgency classification, an importance classification, and one or more extracted keywords;   receiving, from the generative artificial intelligence model, response information comprising the urgency classification, the importance classification, and the one or more extracted keywords;   converting the urgency classification and the importance classification into numerical scores and integrating the numerical scores with output of a classification model that is trained using operation history data;   allocating each data record to one of a plurality of priority queues based on the integrated numerical scores; and   generating, for data records allocated to a first priority queue, output data comprising a condensed text representation produced by the generative artificial intelligence model in accordance with a task-specific prompt sentence, and transmitting the output data to a client terminal via the packet-switched network.

