What is claimed is: 

         1 . A method performed by a permissions management computing platform for securely enabling transactions with an external application without sharing user account data, comprising:
 receiving, by a platform and via a normalized application programming interface (API), a request to authorize use of user account data held by a financial institution computing system having an API specific to the financial institution that enables access to data stored by the financial institution computing system, wherein the request to authorize use of the user account data includes user credentials and one or more permissions limiting access to the use of the user account data by an external application system;   accessing, by the permissions management computing platform, an institution-interface module corresponding to the financial institution computing system, wherein the institution-interface module models the API specific to the financial institution and is generated based on at least one of (i) parsing source code of a first-party application of the financial institution or (ii) parsing communication between the first-party application and the financial institution computing system;   instantiating, by the permissions management computing platform, a software component configured to authenticate with the financial institution computing system as a first-party application of the financial institution, the software component using the institution-interface module to communicate with the financial institution computing system via the API specific to the financial institution;   retrieving, by the platform via the software component, using the user credentials, and via the API specific to the financial institution, the user account data from the financial institution computing system;   formatting, by the permissions management computing platform and using the institution-interface module, the user account data to a normalized format of the normalized API;   generating, by the platform, an electronic record including the user account data and the one or more permissions;   storing, by the platform, the electronic record;   generating, by the platform, a token identifying the electronic record;   transmitting, by the platform and in response to the request to authorize use of the user account data, the token to the external application system;   receiving, by the platform and from the external application system, a request for transaction processing for a transaction associated with a user, wherein the request for transaction processing includes transaction details and the token;   retrieving, by the platform and based on the token, the electronic record;   comparing, by the platform, the transaction details to the one or more permissions in the electronic record to determine whether the external application system is authorized to process the transaction;   determining, by the platform and based on the comparing, that the external application system is authorized to process the transaction; and   processing, by the platform, the transaction requested by the external application system via the software component and using the institution-interface module, the transaction processed using the user account data of the electronic record identified by the token while preventing the external application system from accessing the user account data.   


         2 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the request to authorize use of the user account data is received via a permissions plug-in integrated into the external application system and configured to securely communicate information to the platform. 


         3 . The method of  claim 2 , wherein the permissions plug-in integrated into the external application system prevents access to the user account data by the external application system. 


         4 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the request to authorize use of the user account data further includes selection of an account of the user held by the financial institution computing system to be associated with the external application system. 


         5 . The method of  claim 4 , wherein the user account data includes at least an account number of the selected account of the user and a routing number of the financial institution computing system. 


         6 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the token is generated based on an encrypted hash of one or more elements of the electronic record. 


         7 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the one or more permissions include one or more of: an allowable frequency of transactions, an allowable amount of a transaction, or an allowable type of transaction. 


         8 . The method of  claim 1 , further comprising:
 receiving, by the permissions management computing platform, a request to de-authorize the external application system from initiating transactions associated with the user;   updating the electronic record to reflect the de-authorization; and   in response to a subsequent request for transaction processing received from the external application system that includes the token, returning, by the permissions management computing platform, an indication that the external application system is not authorized to process the subsequent transaction.   


         9 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the institution-interface module further defines headers of messages sent to the financial institution computing system via the API specific to the financial institution computing system. 


         10 . The method of  claim 1 , wherein the software component is configured to authenticate with the financial institution computing system using at least one of (i) an identifier code, (ii) an authentication token, or (iii) a Media Access Control (MAC) address. 


         11 . A permissions management computing platform for securely enabling transactions with an external application without sharing user account data, comprising:
 one or more processors;   a communication interface communicatively coupled to the one or more processors; and   one or more non-transitory memory storing computer-readable instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the permissions management computing platform to:
 receive, via a normalized application programming interface (API), a request to authorize use of user account data held by a financial institution computing system having an API specific to the financial institution computing system that enables access to data stored by the financial institution computing system, wherein the request to authorize use of the user account data includes user credentials and one or more permissions limiting access to the use of the user account data by an external application system; 
 access an institution-interface module corresponding to the financial institution computing system, wherein the institution-interface module models the API specific to the financial institution computing system and is generated based on at least one of (i) parsing source code of a first-party application of the financial institution computing system or (ii) parsing communication between the first-party application and the financial institution computing system; 
 instantiate a software component configured to authenticate with the financial institution computing system as a first-party application of the financial institution computing system, the software component using the institution-interface module to communicate with the financial institution computing system via the API specific to the financial institution computing system; 
 retrieve, via the software component, using the user credentials, and via the API specific to the financial institution computing system, the user account data from the financial institution computing system; 
 format, using the institution-interface module, the user account data to a normalized format of the normalized API; 
 generate an electronic record including the user account data and the one or more permissions; 
 store the electronic record; 
 generate a token identifying the electronic record; 
 transmit, in response to the request to authorize use of the user account data, the token to the external application system; 
 receive, from the external application system, a request for transaction processing for a transaction associated with a user, wherein the request for transaction processing includes transaction details and the token; 
 retrieve, based on the token, the electronic record; 
 compare the transaction details to the one or more permissions in the electronic record to determine whether the external application system is authorized to process the transaction; 
 determine, based on the comparing, that the external application system is authorized to process the transaction; and 
 process the transaction requested by the external application system via the software component and using the institution-interface module, the transaction processed using the user account data of the electronic record identified by the token while preventing the external application system from accessing the user account data. 



