       wherein the rigid frame includes a stabilizing mechanism positioned relative to the thermoformable seal to substantially constrain deformation of the thermoformable seal during molding in cheek regions or upper lip regions; 
       wherein the stabilizing mechanism is configured to provide a positive reference point for location of the mask assembly relative to the patient&#39;s cheek or upper lip to stabilize the mask assembly in a correct posterior and anterior location; 
       wherein adjacent portions of the thermoformable seal are permitted to deform more than the constrained regions during molding; 
       and wherein the rigid frame remains substantially rigid at temperatures below 100° C. 


         9 . The patient interface as claimed in  claim 8 , wherein the thermoformable seal substantially returns toward the non-customized shape after being reheated above its softening temperature, has a hardness greater than 15 Shore D at temperatures between 10° C. and 30° C., and has a hardness below Shore A 10 when heated above its softening temperature. 


         10 . The patient interface as claimed in  claim 8 , wherein at least a portion of the facial-contacting portion of the thermoformable seal is substantially free of silicone or soft elastomer material. 


         11 . The patient interface as claimed in  claim 8 , wherein a substantial portion of the facial-contacting portion of the thermoformable seal is configured to form a sealing interface with the patient&#39;s face without curving inwardly toward the breathing chamber where the thermoformable seal contacts the patient&#39;s face. 


