What is claimed is: 

         1 . A robotic telesurgery portal system comprising:
 a first robotic telesurgery portal at a first location, the first robotic telesurgery portal being couplable to a surgical robot and configured to:
 receive surgical video and robot control feedback data from the surgical robot; 
 synchronize the video and robot control feedback data from the surgical robot; 
 transmit the surgical video and robot control feedback data; 
 receive robot control information for the surgical robot; and 
 communicate robot control information to the surgical robot; 
   a second robotic telesurgery portal at a second location remote from the first location, the second robotic telesurgery portal being couplable to a surgical robot control console and configured to:
 receive surgical video and robot control feedback data from the first robotic telesurgery portal; 
 communicate the received surgical video and robot control feedback data to the surgical robot control console; 
 receive robot control data from the surgical robot control console; and 
 transmit the received robot control data to the first robotic telesurgery portal. 



         2 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 1  wherein the first robotic telesurgery portal and the second robotic telesurgery portal are configured for multiple low-latency modes of secure and redundant communication. 


         3 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 2  wherein the at least one of the low-latency modes of communication is through a 5G cellular communication network. 


         4 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 2  wherein the first robotic telesurgery portal and the second robotic telesurgery portal are configured to prevent the commencement of a surgery until multiple modes of secure and redundant communication are verified. 


         5 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 1  wherein the first robotic telesurgery portal is further configured to synchronize surgical video and robot control feedback data prior to transmitting the surgical video and robot control feedback data. 


         6 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 1  wherein the first robotic telesurgery portal is further configured to encode the surgical video prior to transmitting the surgical video and robot control feedback data. 


         7 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 6  wherein the first robotic telesurgery portal is further configured to variably encode the surgical video depending on sensed communication bandwidth to ensure that sufficient surgical video and robot control feedback data is communicated to the second robotic telesurgery portal. 


         8 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 1  wherein each of the first robotic telesurgery
 portal and the second robotic telesurgery portal further comprise: 
 a microphone; 
 a speaker; 
 a camera; and 
 a display; 
 wherein each of the first robotic telesurgery portal and the second robotic telesurgery portal are further configured to communicate telepresence data received from the microphones and cameras to the speakers and displays. 



         9 . The robotic telesurgery portal system of  claim 1  wherein a single robotic telesurgery portal is configurable as both the first robotic telesurgery portal and the second robotic telesurgery portal.

We claim: 

         1 . A modular geothermal power generation system, comprising 
       a plurality of groups of thermoelectric power generation modules, 
       a hot water supply system; and 
       a cold water supply system; 
       wherein the thermoelectric power generation module comprises at least two heat exchangers, which are arranged adjacent to each other at an interval, the adjacent two heat exchangers are respectively a hot heat exchanger and a cold heat exchanger, a plurality of thermoelectric modules for thermoelectric power generation are arranged between the two heat exchangers, the hot water supply system is connected with the hot heat exchanger, and the cold water supply system is connected with the cold heat exchanger; 
       wherein at least two thermoelectric power generation modules form one power generation group, the heat exchanger comprises a heat dissipation housing, two ends of the heat dissipation housing are respectively provided with a water inlet interface and a water outlet interface, the hot water supply system and the cold water supply system are respectively arranged at left and right sides of the thermoelectric power generation module, the hot water supply system comprises a hot water input pipe and a hot water output pipe, and the cold water supply system comprises a cold water input pipe and a cold water output pipe; 
       the hot heat exchanger and the cold heat exchanger are correspondingly connected between the two adjacent thermoelectric power generation modules in the power generation group through a pipeline, so that the hot heat exchanger and the cold heat exchanger of each thermoelectric power generation module are correspondingly connected in series; the thermoelectric power generation modules located on two sides of the power generation group are a main thermoelectric power generation module and a secondary thermoelectric power generation module, the water inlet interface of the hot heat exchanger of the main thermoelectric power generation module is connected with the hot water input pipe through a pipeline, and the water outlet interface of the hot heat exchanger of the secondary thermoelectric power generation module is connected with the hot water output pipe through a pipeline; the water inlet interface of the cold heat exchanger of the main thermoelectric power generation module is connected with the cold water input pipe through a pipeline, and the water outlet interface of the cold heat exchanger of the secondary thermoelectric power generation module is connected with the cold water output pipe through a pipeline; 
       the heat dissipation housing comprises a cover plate and a bottom shell, the bottom shell comprises a bottom plate, a middle part of the bottom plate is provided with a plurality of ribs arranged at intervals, the ribs are arranged along a length direction of the heat exchanger to divide an internal space of the heat exchanger into a plurality of channels, and the water inlet interface and the water outlet interface are respectively arranged at a lower end of a left side and an upper end of a right side of the heat dissipation housing; 
       the thermoelectric power generation module comprises 2K+1 heat exchangers, and K is a natural number, wherein K heat exchangers are the hot heat exchangers; K+1 heat exchangers are the cold heat exchangers, and the hot heat exchanger is arranged between two adjacent cold heat exchangers; the thermoelectric power generation module further comprises a fixing structure for fixing the heat exchanger, and the fixing structure comprises two clamping plates, which are fixedly connected through a connecting piece; 
       both a left side plate and a right side plate of the bottom shell are arranged obliquely; a distance between a left end face of the rib and the left side plate increases gradually from top to bottom, and a distance between a right end face of the rib and the right side plate decreases gradually from top to bottom; 
       the two thermoelectric power generation modules form one power generation group, the hot water input pipe and the hot water output pipe are located at a front end and a back end of one side of the thermoelectric power generation module, the cold water input pipe and the cold water output pipe are located at a front end and a back end of the other side of the thermoelectric power generation module, a side face of the hot water input pipe is connected with a plurality of hot water input manifolds which are transversely arranged, the hot water input manifold is connected with the water inlet interface of the hot heat exchanger through a pipeline, the hot water output pipe is connected with a plurality of hot water output manifolds which are transversely arranged, the hot water output manifold is connected with the water outlet interface of the hot heat exchanger through a pipeline, the hot water input manifolds and the hot water output manifolds are alternately arranged; a side face of the cold water input pipe is connected with a plurality of cold water input manifolds which are transversely arranged, the cold water input manifold is connected with the water inlet interface of the cold heat radiator through a pipeline, the cold water output pipe is connected with a plurality of cold water output manifolds which are transversely arranged, the cold water output manifold is connected with the water outlet interface of the cold heat exchanger through a pipeline; and the cold water input manifolds and the cold water output manifolds are alternately arranged; and 
       the two thermoelectric power generation modules form one power generation group, so that the cold water input pipe and the cold water output pipe are located at the same side, while the hot water input pipe and the hot water output pipe are located at the same side, which is convenient to manage; secondly, the cold water input manifolds and the cold water output manifolds are alternately arranged; and the hot water input manifolds and the hot water output manifolds are alternately arranged, so that a space is reasonably utilized. 


         2 . The modular geothermal power generation system according to  claim 1 , wherein the modular geothermal power generation system further comprises a bracket for fixing the thermoelectric power generation module; the bracket comprises a bottom plate, a supporting plate is arranged in a middle part of the bottom plate, two side faces of the supporting plate are respectively connected with a plurality of bearing plates arranged at intervals, and the thermoelectric power generation module is fixed on the bearing plates. 


         3 . The modular geothermal power generation system according to  claim 1 , further comprising a box body, wherein the thermoelectric power generation module, the cold water supply system, the hot water supply system and the bracket are all arranged in the box body, and an outer side of the box body is provided with an interface connected with the cold water supply system and an interface connected with the hot water supply system. 


         4 . The modular geothermal power generation system according to  claim 3 , wherein a control system is arranged at an upper end of the box body, and the control system is used for monitoring a working state of the cold water supply system, a working state of the hot water supply system and a working state of the thermoelectric power generation module.

1 . An apparatus for producing water from ambient humidity, comprising a solar receiver, the solar receiver comprising:
 a frame;   a reflective surface which is configured to reflect solar radiation and which is fixed to the frame; the reflective surface having a focusing axis for theincident solar radiation;   a thermal absorber which is transparent to solar radiation and which is positioned substantially in the region of the focusing axis; the thermal absorber;   
       the apparatus further comprising:
 a casing which is in fluid dynamic communication with the thermal absorber so as to generate a working circuit; 
 an intake valve which connects the casing to the external environment through a respective intake opening which opens from the casing and which is configured to allow the introduction of air from the external environment into the working circuit; 
 an emission valve which connects the casing to the external environment through a respective emission opening which opens from the casing and which is configured to allow the emission of air from the working circuit; 
 a condenser which is connected to the casing; 
 a drying material which is arranged inside the casing; 
 a device for the forced circulation of air which is connected, in fluid-dynamic terms, to the casing and to the solar absorber, the device for the forced circulation of air being configured so as to generate an incoming air current and/or an outgoing air current into/from the casing; 
 the intake valve and emission valve being selectively actuatable from an open configuration to a closed configuration, and vice versa, so as to allow in a selective and reversible manner the fluid-dynamic connection between the drying material and surrounding humid air, which is present in the external environment, or between the drying material and warm air and/or vapor which are contained in the working circuit and heated by the thermal absorber so as to carry out an adsorption cycle of the humidity by the drying material and a desorption cycle of water vapor from the drying material, respectively; 

       wherein the device for the forced circulation of air is configured to operate according to two operating configurations, a first configuration, in which the intake valve and the emission valve are open and the device for the forced circulation of air generates the air current which is introduced into the casing so that there takes place the adsorption cycle of the humidity by the drying material, and a second configuration, in which the valves are closed and the desorption cycle of water vapor by the drying material takes place by means of forced circulation of the warm air and/or the vapor in the working circuit, through the thermal absorber and the drying material, the forced circulation being obtained by means of the device for the forced circulation of air. 


         2 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 1 , wherein the casing is concentric with respect to the solar absorber and which is transparent to solar radiation and the thermal absorber is contained in the casing. 


         3 . The apparatus according to  claim 1 , wherein the solar receiver is a convection-type solar receiver and wherein the casing extends longitudinally between an intake end and an emission end and contains the drying material, the casing being subdivided, transversely relative to the longitudinal extent thereof, by at least one perforated partition wall, the perforated partition wall permitting passage of the air and water vapor. 


         4 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 2 , wherein the thermal absorber extends longitudinally between a respective intake end and a respective emission end and contains the drying material, the thermal absorber being subdivided, transversely relative to the longitudinal extent thereof, by at least one perforated partition wall, the perforated partition wall permitting passage of the air and water vapor. 


         5 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 1 , further comprising at least one photovoltaic panel which is fixed to the frame, the photovoltaic panel configured to supply electrical energy to electromechanical elements. 


         6 . The apparatus for producing water according to claims  claim 1 , wherein the thermal absorber has an opaque coating. 


         7 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 1 , wherein the thermal absorber has a spectrally selective coating, with high absorbance of solar radiation and high reflectance of infrared thermal radiation. 


         8 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 1 , further comprising a tank which is connected to the condenser in order to receive the water which is conveyed inside the condenser and which is released as water vapor from the drying material. 


         9 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 1 , further comprising a pump for extracting the vapor which is connected to the condenser. 


         10 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 1 , further comprising at least one sensor selected from: a temperature sensor proximate to the drying material; an input temperature sensor in a region of the intake end; an output temperature sensor in a region of the emission end; a pressure sensor proximate to the drying material; a humidity sensor proximate to the drying material; an incoming humidity sensor in a region of the intake end; an outgoing humidity sensor in a region of the emission end; a load cell; or an optical sensor which is provided to distinguish daylight hours from night-time hours or hours without sunshine. 


         11 .- 16 . (canceled) 


         17 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 10 , further comprising a support device which is configured to rotationally secure the solar receiver with respect to a support plane. 


         18 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 17 , further comprising a control unit which is electrically connected to the intake valve, the emission valve and the device for the forced circulation so as to selectively carry out the adsorption cycle and the desorption cycle. 


         19 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 18 , further comprising a control unit which is electrically connected to at least one or more of the sensors and capable of processing thesignals coming from the at least one sensor and actuating the valves by opening or closing them in accordance with requirements and activating or deactivating the device for the forced circulation of air. 


         20 . The apparatus for producing water according to  claim 18 , wherein the control unit is controls motors and/or actuators configured to move the support and the solar receiver on the support. 


         21 . The apparatus for producing water from ambient humidity according to  claim 20 , further comprising a hydroponic or aeroponic greenhouse device which is connected to the solar receiver. 


         22 . A method for producing water from the ambient humidity by means of an apparatus for producing water according to  claim 1 , the method comprising:
 carrying out a forced air circulation so as to introduce humid air which is present in the surrounding environment inside the drying material suitable for absorbing the humidity;   isolating, in fluid-dynamic terms, the working circuit from the exterior, generating a fluid-dynamically closed circuit between the thermal absorber and the casing;   heating the air which is contained in the thermal absorber and in the casing by means of the reflective surface which is contained in the solar receiver;   carrying out a forced circulation of air inside the working circuit so as to desorb the adsorbed water on the drying material both by conduction, through thetransmission of heat by contact, and by convection, carrying out the forced circulation of air and water vapor as a thermovector fluid;   collecting the water vapor from the fluid-dynamically closed circuit in a condenser which is connected to a tank;   repeating the preceding operations until thea desired water quantity is obtained.   


         23 . AThe method according to  claim 22 , wherein the apparatus further comprises an optical sensor which is provided to distinguish daylight hours from night-time hours or hours without sunshine, and wherein the method further comprises comprising:
 processing the signal of the optical sensor;   if the signal corresponds to daylight hours, changing from the adsorption cycle to the desorption cycle; if the signal corresponds to night-time hours or hours without sunshine, changing from the desorption cycle to the adsorption cycle.   


         24 . AThe method according to  claim 23 , wherein the apparatus further comprises a load cell and a temperature sensor, and wherein the method further comprises:
 carrying out a first measurement of the weight of the apparatus with the load cell;   carrying out forced circulation of the air so as to circulate humid air which is present in the surrounding environment inside the drying material suitable for absorbing humidity;   periodically carrying out a second measurement of the weight of the apparatus until a predetermined threshold is reached;   once the predetermined threshold is reached, processing the signal of the optical sensor;   if the signal corresponds to daylight hours, isolating the apparatus from the exterior in fluid-dynamic terms, generating a fluid-dynamically closed circuit between the thermal absorber and the casing;   interrupting the forced circulation of air;   heating the air which is contained in the thermal absorber and in the casing by means of the reflective surface contained in the solar receiver;   carrying out periodic temperature measurements until a predetermined temperature is reached;   activating the forced circulation of air;   periodically carrying out a third measurement of the weight of the receivers;   desorbing the adsorbed water on the drying material both by conduction, through the transmission of heat by contact, and by convection, carrying out the forced circulation of air and water vapor as a thermovector fluid;   
       collecting the water vapor from the fluid-dynamically closed circuit in a condenser which is connected to a tank; 
       when the third measurement reaches the first measurement, interrupting the vapor collection; 
       repeating the preceding operations until the desired water quantity is obtained.

