What is claimed is: 

         1 . A device for enhancing electrical connectivity of an electrical ground path in a coaxial cable connector comprising:
 an enhanced coaxial cable connector assembly comprising:
 a connector body structurally arranged to have a rearward cable receiving end and a forward end opposite the rearward cable receiving end; 
 a nose portion structurally arranged to have a rearward end and a forward end, wherein the rearward end is structurally arranged to be coupled with the forward end of the connector body; 
 a coupler structurally arranged to be coupled with the forward end of the nose portion; 
 a post disposed within at least a portion of the connector body and the nose portion; 
 a first wave shaped biasing portion structurally arranged to be received by at least a portion of a receiving groove in an outer surface at the forward end of the nose portion; 
 a second wave shaped biasing portion that is structurally arranged to be received in the receiving groove; 
   wherein the coupler is structurally arranged to be rotatably coupled to the nose portion;   wherein the coupler has an inward radial protrusion structurally arranged to extend radially inwardly, and the inward radial protrusion has a forward radial wall and a rearward radial wall;   wherein the first wave shaped biasing portion has a front radial surface and a rear radial surface and is structurally arranged to form less than a complete circle;   wherein the first wave shaped biasing portion is structurally arranged to have an undulating shape when not axially compressed such that the front and rear radial surfaces of the first wave shaped biasing portion are not planar surfaces;   wherein the first wave shaped biasing portion is structurally arranged to have an inner diameter that is less than an outer diameter of the receiving groove when the first wave shaped biasing portion is not mounted in the receiving groove;   wherein the first wave shaped biasing portion is structurally arranged such that a portion of the front radial surface of the first wave shaped biasing portion contacts the rearward radial wall of the inward radial protrusion while simultaneously a portion of the rear radial surface of the first wave shaped biasing portion contacts a rearward radial wall of the receiving groove so as to retain the coupler on the connector body; and   wherein the first wave shaped biasing portion is structurally arranged to provide an electrical ground path between the nose portion and the coupler so as to improve an electrically conductive connection between an outer conductor of a coaxial cable and the coupler when the coupler is not connected to an interface port, when the coupler is loosely coupled to the interface port, and when the coupler is fully tightened to the interface port;   wherein the second wave shaped biasing portion is structurally arranged to include a front radial surface and a rear radial surface and is configured to form less than a complete circle;   wherein the second wave shaped biasing portion is structurally arranged to have an undulating shape when at rest such that the front and rear radial surfaces of the second wave shaped biasing portion are not planar surfaces;   wherein the second wave shaped biasing portion is structurally arranged to have an inner diameter that is less than the outer diameter of the receiving groove when the second wave spring shaped biasing portion is not mounted in the receiving groove; and   wherein the coaxial cable connector assembly is structurally arranged to provide enhanced electrical conductivity of the electrical ground path by structurally arranging the second wave shaped biasing portion such that a portion of the rear radial surface of the second wave shaped biasing portion contacts the forward radial wall of the inward radial protrusion while simultaneously a portion of the front radial surface of the second wave shaped biasing portion contacts a forward radial wall of the receiving groove so as to retain the coupler on the connector body.   


         2 . The device of  claim 1 , wherein the first wave shaped biasing portion comprises a first wave spring, and the second wave shaped biasing portion comprises a second wave spring. 


         3 . The device of  claim 1 , wherein the second wave shaped biasing portion is configured to provide an electrical ground path between the nose portion and the coupler so as to improve an electrically conductive connection between an outer conductor of a coaxial cable and the coupler when the coupler is not connected to an interface port, when the coupler is loosely coupled to the interface port, and when the coupler is fully tightened to the interface port.

