 g_Lachnospira; 
 f_Corynebacteriaceae; 
 g_Corynebacterium; 
 o_Actinomycetales; 
 f Paraprevotellaceae; 
 g_Eubacterium; 
 g_Peptoniphilus; 
 o_Enterobacteriales; 
 c_Erysipelotrichi; 
 c_Gammaproteobacteria; 
 g_Finegoldia; 
 p_Proteobacteria, 
 f Bacteroidaceae; and 
 c_Deltaproteobacteria; 
   (c) generating a numerical microbiome score from the genetic analysis performed in (b);   (d) comparing the numerical microbiome score generated in (c) with a predetermined reference value which delineates a cutoff between (i) clinically significant cancer and (ii) low-risk cancer/negative biopsy, so as to determine if the gut microbiome sample is associated with a clinically significant cancer,   wherein a numerical microbiome score equal to or greater than the predetermined reference value indicates the sample comes from a human subject at risk of clinically significant cancer and a numerical microbiome score less than the predetermined reference value indicates the sample comes from a human subject with low-risk of cancer/negative biopsy.   


