What is claimed is: 

         1 ) A computer system ( 100 ) for aiding in decision-making in a situation involving one or more users, the system ( 100 ) comprising:
 a) a plurality of input devices comprising one or more cameras, one or more microphones, one or more physiological sensors, and one or more text-input interface devices, each input device configured to accept a plurality of inputs from the one or more users, each input of the plurality of inputs comprising measurements of one or more physiological parameters, measurements of one or more environmental parameters, and one or more user inputs comprising one or more user-proposed actions;   b) a cloud server ( 120 ) communicatively coupled to the plurality of input devices comprising:
 i) a behavior-based user profile associated with a decision-making user of the one or more users; 
 ii) a semiotic database ( 123 ) comprising a plurality of terms, each term comprising one or more weighted emotional meanings, each weighted emotional meaning comprising a meaning of the term corresponding to a context and a tone, and a weight value corresponding to an emotional weight of the term given the context and the tone, and one or more relationships between the term and other terms of the semiotic database ( 123 ) based on the context and the tone; 
 iii) a data pre-processing module ( 124 ) comprising computer-readable instructions for:
 A) receiving the plurality of inputs from the one or more users; 
 B) identifying a plurality of terms in the one or more user inputs; 
 C) deriving one or more physiological descriptive terms corresponding to the measurements of the one or more physiological parameters and one or more environmental descriptive terms corresponding to the measurements of the one or more environmental parameters, wherein the one or more physiological descriptive terms and the one or more environmental descriptive terms are incorporated into the plurality of terms; 
 D) estimating, based on the plurality of terms and the semiotic database ( 123 ), an estimated context based on corresponding contexts according to relationships between the plurality of terms as the plurality of terms appear in the semiotic database ( 123 ); and 
 E) estimating, based on the plurality of inputs and the semiotic database ( 123 ), an estimated tone of each user based on corresponding tones according to relationships between the plurality of terms as the plurality of terms appear in the semiotic database ( 123 ) and the estimated context; 

 iv) a decision Artificial Intelligence (AI) model ( 125 ) associated with the behavior-based user profile, trained by existing decision-making data comprising relationships between contexts and tones and quality of decision-making, configured to accept the plurality of inputs, the estimated context, and the estimated tone, identify one or more decision-making impediments in the plurality of inputs;
 wherein the decision AI model ( 125 ) is further trained by past decisions made by the decision-making user and outputs thereof, such that the decision AI model ( 125 ) provides personalized aid to the decision-making user; 

 v) a database AI model ( 126 ) communicatively coupled to the decision AI model ( 125 ), trained by a database of known impediments to optimal decision making and thinking, configured to accept the one or more decision-making impediments from the decision AI model ( 125 ) and generate one or more decision-enhancing suggestions comprising one or more AI proposed actions, a decision quality assessment, sets of data and information supporting a recommended decision, a list of potential implications of the one or more user proposed actions, and a list of potential implications of the one or more AI proposed actions as output; and 
 vi) computer-readable instructions for:
 A) accepting the plurality of inputs from the plurality of input devices; 
 B) inputting the plurality of inputs from the plurality of input devices into the data pre-processing module ( 124 ); 
 C) inputting the plurality of inputs, the estimated context, and the estimated tone into the decision AI model ( 125 ); and 
 D) inputting the one or more decision-making impediments into the database AI model ( 126 ); 

   b) a processor ( 130 ) communicatively coupled to the cloud server ( 120 ) and the plurality of input devices, configured to execute computer-readable instructions; and   c) a memory component operatively coupled to the processor ( 130 ), comprising computer-readable instructions for:
 i) receiving the plurality of inputs from the plurality of input devices; 
 ii) transmitting the plurality of inputs to the cloud server ( 120 ); 
 iii) receiving the one or more decision-enhancing suggestions; and 
 iv) displaying the one or more decision-enhancing suggestions to the one or more users. 



